# Topic data is byte-exact: sources are hashed, and JSON and JSONL files are canonical bytes. Every checkout keeps LF
# line endings whatever core.autocrlf says, and stored source texts (and kept originals) are never converted at all.
# Every topic rule matches at any depth, so a topic made with `onto init --path <folder>` below the git root keeps
# its hashes and its log merges too.
* text=auto eol=lf
**/sources/** -text
# Append-only topic logs and the local questions (one question per line) merge by keeping both sides' lines; the
# graph files and the local pack do not, so git shows real conflicts (AGENTS.md, "Merging topic branches", says how
# to resolve them, and how to settle two questions added under one id).
**/interview/log.jsonl merge=union
**/ledger/changes.jsonl merge=union
**/metrics/history.jsonl merge=union
**/sources/index.jsonl merge=union
**/packs/local.questions.jsonl merge=union
